# The apply image's build context is the repo root (docker/apply/Dockerfile, Phase 23). BuildKit
# reads this file, and not the root .dockerignore, because it sits beside that Dockerfile under the
# Dockerfile's own name: the sync image's allow-list (the root file) is not touched.
#
# An allow-list: only the folders that Dockerfile copies from are sent. Of workspace/ only src/
# goes, because the worker's bundle is built from apply/src and the Phase 21 modules it imports.
# Every node_modules, dist and coverage folder and every .env file stay out, so nothing host-built
# and nothing secret reaches a layer. The pinned CA comes from the named context `harness-certs`.
*
!docker/apply/
!apply/
!workspace/src/
!mcp-server/
!skills/inbox-apply/
!skills/announcement-review/
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
